      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we compute the log-likelihood as the mean over pixel dimensions (rather than the sum) and rescale the result by a factor κ−1",
      "bbox": [
        55.08201599121094,
        350.4576721191406,
        541.7416381835938,
        361.4549255371094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(where κ = 104). We use a resampling threshold such that we resample if the ESS is less than N = 32. We train the neural",
      "bbox": [
        55.11201477050781,
        362.8031921386719,
        541.4439086914062,
        373.409912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "networks for 3000 iterations. The learnable parameters are updated using the Adam optimiser (learning rate 10−4) with",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        374.3676452636719,
        541.442138671875,
        385.36590576171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "global gradient clipping (maximum norm 1.0) and β2 = 0.999 (other Adam defaults as in Optax). We use N = 32 particles",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        388.2549743652344,
        541.4405517578125,
        398.5957336425781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to approximate the negative log-likelihood during training.",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        400.3693542480469,
        289.12261962890625,
        409.2759094238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the second setting, we consider a more challenging regime in which we force resampling at every filtering step after",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        418.3023681640625,
        541.6135864257812,
        427.20892333984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j > 10. Here, we use process noise with Λζ = σ2",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        428.5561828613281,
        253.29908752441406,
        440.438720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ζ diag(0, 1) with σ2",
      "bbox": [
        248.96702575683594,
        428.5561828613281,
        330.2560729980469,
        441.7657470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ζ = 0.1, and make an additive noise assumption in the",
      "bbox": [
        325.9229736328125,
        430.09796142578125,
        541.4418334960938,
        441.7657470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "learned transition model. We use σtrain = 5 σobs and no other scaling of the log-likelihood compared to the true observation",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        442.052978515625,
        541.44189453125,
        452.6129150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model. We train the neural networks for 1500 iterations. The learnable parameters are updated using the Adam optimiser",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        454.1673583984375,
        541.6065063476562,
        463.07391357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(learning rate 2 × 10−4) with global gradient clipping (maximum norm 1.0) and β2 = 0.99 (other Adam defaults as in",
      "bbox": [
        55.11201477050781,
        464.03167724609375,
        541.44189453125,
        482.44110107421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Optax). Here, we use N = 16 particles. The optimiser omits at most 10 consecutive non-finite parameter updates by leaving",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        477.91796875,
        541.4415283203125,
        486.9839172363281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the current parameter values unchanged.",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        490.0333557128906,
        216.47544860839844,
        498.9399108886719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Results and evaluation",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        516.90380859375,
        152.51576232910156,
        525.8601684570312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We evaluate the learnt models by comparing the average SSIM and PSNR of image sequences",
      "bbox": [
        162.47715759277344,
        517.0233764648438,
        541.4429931640625,
        525.929931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obtained by unrolling the dynamics from Z0 using the learnt transition function fθ, and then generating images by passing",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        528.8189697265625,
        541.4427490234375,
        539.3799438476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the resulting state trajectory through the learnt decoder rϕ. All results corresponding to the first experiment setting are",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        540.77392578125,
        541.4404907226562,
        550.535888671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "averaged over 5 independent runs, and all results corresponding to the second experiment setting are averaged over 9",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        552.7299194335938,
        541.6893310546875,
        561.7958984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "independent runs.",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001770019531,
        564.8443603515625,
        126.27408599853516,
        573.7509155273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For the first setting, results for different configurations of the diffusion resampler are presented in Table 13. Results for",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        582.7763671875,
        541.6138916015625,
        591.6829223632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "different configurations of the baselines are presented in Table 14. For the second, more challenging setting, in which",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        594.7323608398438,
        541.4407958984375,
        603.638916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "resampling is invoked at nearly every filtering step, the corresponding results are presented in Tables 15 and 16, respectively.",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        606.6873779296875,
        543.1870727539062,
        615.5939331054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 8 shows the median loss evolution during training for the best model configuration (in terms of mean SSIM and",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        618.642333984375,
        541.4411010742188,
        627.5488891601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PSNR) from each resampling class in each experiment setting. Figure 9 shows mean prediction SSIM/PSNR for the second",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        630.5973510742188,
        541.439208984375,
        639.50390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "setting; see Figure 5 for a comparison to the corresponding results in the first setting.",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        642.5523681640625,
        393.3115234375,
        651.4589233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The difference in SSIM/PSNR between the two experiments indicate that the second setting is more challenging for all",
      "bbox": [
        55.13101577758789,
        660.4853515625,
        541.4368286132812,
        669.3919067382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "resampling methods. In the first setting, performance is competitive, and diffusion resampling provides a stable end-to-end",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        672.4403686523438,
        541.4368286132812,
        681.346923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "optimisation and effective integration into the high-dimensional learning pipeline. Notably, resampling is not always",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        684.3953857421875,
        541.4408569335938,
        693.3019409179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "necessary for convergence in end-to-end training using particle filters, and prior work has reported cases where omitting",
      "bbox": [
        55.44001388549805,
        696.3513793945312,
        541.4412231445312,
        705.2579345703125
      ],
      "direction": [
